<title>UK: Storehouse down, SBC Warburg cuts estimates.</title>
<headline>Storehouse down, SBC Warburg cuts estimates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Storehouse Plc dropped against the trend of a strong UK retail sector on Wednesday as analysts at SBC Warburg lowered earnings estimates, dealers said.</p>
<p>Analysts at Warburg were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Sources said the downgrade reflected trading conditions at key units such as British Home Stores.</p>
<p>The stock was down 10p at 235-1/2 by 1236 GMT in volume of 3.2 million shares.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
